 ## Overview
-This family addresses the dependency on external Structure-from-Motion (SfM) pipelines and iterative per-scene optimization in standard 3D Gaussian Splatting. It enables reconstruction from uncalibrated images either by eliminating iterative camera optimization in favor of geometric priors (pose-free) or by replacing the optimization loop entirely with a direct neural mapping from images to Gaussians (feed-forward). It distinguishes itself from standard iterative methods by removing the need for known camera poses and reducing training time from minutes to seconds or milliseconds.
+This family enables 3D Gaussian Splatting reconstruction without iterative per-scene optimization or known camera poses. It solves the dependency on Structure-from-Motion (SfM) pipelines and slow differentiable rendering loops by using neural networks to directly predict Gaussian primitives from images [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard [3D Gaussian Splatting Training](3761-3d-gaussian-splatting-training.md) which requires known poses and iterative gradient descent, these methods are either feed-forward (instant inference) or use fixed priors to bypass pose learning [S1, unofficial].
 
